FC-08 — Company & User–Company Relationships

Version: 3.2.3
Status: Implementation-Ready / TDD-Ready
Date: 30 August 2026
Type: Feature Contract / Intermediate Architecture & Implementation Specification
Project: Foresy
Authors: Senior Product Architect + CTO

1. Purpose

FC-08 defines the domain, data model, business rules, API contract, and implementation constraints for managing:

Companies
User–Company relationships
Company roles
Company lifecycle
Company legal and administrative information
The onboarding case where a User does not yet have an active Company

FC-08 establishes the structural foundation required for future Foresy features involving:

independent activity
client activity
missions
CRA
forecasting
simulation
fiscal and regulatory consequences

FC-08 does not implement fiscal calculation, forecasting, simulation, or CRA evolution.

2. Product Context

Foresy is a backend-first SaaS product for independent professionals.

The product must allow a User to:

register without having a Company;
explore and simulate possible professional situations;
subsequently create or register a Company;
operate through one or more Companies;
act in different capacities depending on the Company relationship;
maintain a distinction between independent activity and client activity.

A User therefore does not intrinsically have a single global business role.

The role is contextual to the relationship between a User and a Company.

