18.1 Existing Fields

Existing fields not introduced or structurally changed by FC-08 are retained.

FC-08 does not rename:

name

to:

legal_name

The existing name field is the canonical Company name field for FC-08.

19. Company Field Rules
19.1 name

Required.

A Company cannot exist without a name.

19.2 siren

Required.

The SIREN must:

be present;
contain a valid French SIREN format;
be unique.
19.3 siret

Optional at database level.

Multiple Companies may have NULL SIRET values.

A non-null SIRET must be unique.

FC-08 does not introduce contextual rules requiring SIRET in particular business situations.

19.4 legal_form

Nullable.

The legal form may be unknown or not yet available when the Company is created.

The field is stored as a string.

FC-08 does not implement the INSEE legal-form nomenclature itself.

19.5 tax_number

Optional contextual tax identifier.

No fiscal calculation is performed by FC-08.

19.6 Address

Address fields are stored as Company data.

FC-08 does not implement address verification.

19.7 country

Default:

FR
19.8 currency

Default:

EUR
19.9 vat_regime

Stored as a string.

FC-08 treats VAT regime as contextual Company information.

It does not implement VAT calculations.

20. Legal Form

The Company legal form is stored using:

legal_form

The value is a string.

FC-08 does not replace this with a PostgreSQL enum.

FC-08 does not create a versioned INSEE nomenclature table.

Future integration with official INSEE/INPI referentials may introduce:

validated legal-form codes;
nomenclature versions;
synchronization;
provenance;
official source metadata.

Those capabilities are outside FC-08 MVP.

