34. Company Creation Principle

Company creation and the initial UserCompany relationship must be atomic.

The main onboarding operation is:

POST /companies

with:

Company data
+
role

The operation must execute in a single database transaction.

Either:

Company + UserCompany

are both created,

or:

neither is persisted.
35. Company Creation Flow

The expected flow is:

POST /companies
       │
       ▼
Validate Company
       │
       ▼
Create Company
       │
       ▼
Create UserCompany
       │
       ▼
Commit transaction

If any step fails:

ROLLBACK
36. Company API
36.1 List Companies
GET /companies

Returns Companies accessible through active UserCompany relationships.

36.2 Create Company
POST /companies

Creates:

Company
UserCompany

atomically.

36.3 Show Company
GET /companies/:id

Returns a Company accessible to the authenticated User.

36.4 Update Company
PATCH /companies/:id

Updates permitted Company attributes.

Authorization must be based on the authenticated User's active relationship with the Company.

36.5 Delete Company
DELETE /companies/:id

Performs soft deletion.

Physical deletion is not performed.

37. UserCompany API
37.1 List Relationships
GET /user_companies

Returns relationships belonging to the authenticated User.

37.2 Create Relationship
POST /user_companies

Allows a new role to be added to an existing Company.

This endpoint does not replace the atomic onboarding endpoint.

37.3 Update Relationship
PATCH /user_companies/:id

The MVP permits modification of:

role

only.

The following must not be modifiable through this endpoint:

user_id
company_id
deleted_at
37.4 Delete Relationship
DELETE /user_companies/:id

Soft-deletes the relationship.

