55. Acceptance Criteria — Gherkin
Scenario 1 — User has no Company
Given an authenticated User with no Company relationship
When the User requests their Companies
Then the API returns an empty collection
And no Company is created automatically
Scenario 2 — Create Company as Independent
Given an authenticated User
When the User creates a Company with role "independent"
Then the Company is created
And a UserCompany relationship is created
And the relationship role is "independent"
Scenario 3 — Create Company as Client
Given an authenticated User
When the User creates a Company with role "client"
Then the Company is created
And a UserCompany relationship is created
And the relationship role is "client"
Scenario 4 — Multiple Companies
Given an authenticated User
And the User already has a relationship with Company A
When the User creates Company B
Then Company B is created
And both Companies are accessible to the User
Scenario 5 — Multiple Roles With Same Company
Given a User has an "independent" relationship with Company A
When the User adds a "client" relationship with Company A
Then the second relationship is created
And both roles coexist
Scenario 6 — Duplicate Role
Given a User has an "independent" relationship with Company A
When the User attempts to create another "independent" relationship with Company A
Then the request is rejected
And no duplicate relationship is created
Scenario 7 — Fictitious Company
Given an authenticated User without a Company
When the User accesses Foresy
Then no fictitious Company is created
And the User may continue without a Company
Scenario 8 — Invalid SIREN
Given an authenticated User
When the User creates a Company with an invalid SIREN
Then the request is rejected
And the Company is not created
And the UserCompany relationship is not created
Scenario 9 — Duplicate SIREN
Given Company A already exists with SIREN "123456789"
When the User creates another Company with SIREN "123456789"
Then the request is rejected
And no duplicate Company is created
Scenario 10 — SIRET Absent
Given an authenticated User
When the User creates a Company without a SIRET
Then the Company is created
And the SIRET is NULL
Scenario 11 — Duplicate SIRET
Given Company A already exists with SIRET "12345678900012"
When the User creates another Company with SIRET "12345678900012"
Then the request is rejected
And no duplicate Company is created
Scenario 12 — Atomicity
Given an authenticated User
When Company creation succeeds but UserCompany creation fails
Then the transaction is rolled back
And no Company remains persisted
And no UserCompany remains persisted
Scenario 13 — Unauthorized Company Access
Given a Company belonging to another User
When the authenticated User attempts to access that Company
Then the request is rejected
And the response uses the standardized API error format
Scenario 14 — Soft Delete
Given an active Company
When the Company is deleted
Then deleted_at is populated
And the Company is excluded from Company.active
And the Company remains persisted
Scenario 15 — Flat JSON Parameters
Given an authenticated User
When the User submits Company attributes as flat JSON
And provides role separately
Then the request is processed correctly
And the Company attributes are wrapped under Company parameters
And role is processed as a UserCompany attribute
