FC-08 Architectural Invariants
INV-01 — Company Has No User FK

Company must never contain:

user_id
INV-02 — User Has No Company FK

User must never contain:

company_id
INV-03 — UserCompany Is the Relationship

User–Company relationships must be represented by UserCompany.

INV-04 — User Can Exist Without Company

A User may have zero UserCompany records.

INV-05 — No Fictitious Company

Absence of Company must never be represented by a fake Company record.

INV-06 — Role Is Contextual

Role belongs to UserCompany, not User.

INV-07 — SIREN Is Mandatory

Every Company must have a SIREN.

INV-08 — SIREN Is Valid

Every Company SIREN must satisfy the implemented SIREN validation rules.

INV-09 — SIREN Is Unique

Two Companies cannot have the same SIREN.

INV-10 — SIREN Is Present, Valid and Unique

The SIREN must simultaneously satisfy presence, validity, and uniqueness constraints.

INV-11 — SIRET Is Nullable

A Company may have no SIRET.

INV-12 — SIRET Is Unique When Present

Two Companies cannot share the same non-null SIRET.

INV-13 — VAT Regime Is Contextual

vat_regime stores context only.

It does not implement fiscal calculation.

INV-14 — Legal Form Is Contextual

legal_form stores Company legal-form information only.

INV-15 — No Fictitious Legal Entity for Simulation

Simulation must not create a real Company record.

INV-16 — Atomic Company Onboarding

Company creation and initial UserCompany creation are atomic.

INV-17 — No Partial Onboarding

A failed onboarding transaction must not leave an orphan Company.

INV-18 — Relationship Role Uniqueness

The same User, Company and Role combination may exist only once.

INV-19 — Explicit Active Scope

Active records must be queried through explicit lifecycle scopes.

INV-20 — No Default Scope

No default scope may be used to implement lifecycle behavior.

INV-21 — Soft Delete

Company and UserCompany deletion must use deleted_at.

INV-22 — Role Is Outside Company Wrapping

The Company parameter wrapper must not absorb role.

Final Architectural Position

FC-08 establishes the Company and User–Company relationship foundation without attempting to solve future domains prematurely.

The resulting conceptual model is:

                    ┌──────────────┐
                    │     User     │
                    │              │
                    │ id: bigint   │
                    └──────┬───────┘
                           │
                           │ user_id
                           ▼
                    ┌──────────────┐
                    │ UserCompany  │
                    │              │
                    │ id: uuid     │
                    │ role         │
                    │ deleted_at   │
                    └──────┬───────┘
                           │
                           │ company_id
                           ▼
                    ┌──────────────┐
                    │   Company    │
                    │              │
                    │ id: uuid     │
                    │ name         │
                    │ siren        │
                    │ siret        │
                    │ legal_form   │
                    │ vat_regime   │
                    │ ...          │
                    └──────────────┘

This model supports:

User
 ├── Company A / independent
 ├── Company A / client
 ├── Company B / independent
 └── Company C / client

while preserving the critical distinction between:

the User;
the Company;
the relationship;
the role;
the activity performed through that relationship.

FC-08 deliberately does not solve:

fiscal calculations;
regulatory calculations;
simulation;
forecasting;
CRA evolution;
Mission activity separation;
INSEE/INPI synchronization;
field-level provenance.

Those concerns remain available for future Feature Contracts without requiring a structural refactoring of the Company/UserCompany foundation.
